Bugfix: Name the delete button of the group list

Every group in the user management carried a delete control with no accessible
name, even though the markup looked like it had one: it used an original-title
attribute. That attribute is not standardised and nothing in the code base reads
it - the tooltip library looks at title and data-original-title only, and no
tooltip is initialised on the group list in the first place. So it provided
neither a name for assistive technology nor a tooltip for a mouse user.

The only other candidate was an img without an alt attribute, which cannot
supply a name either. The control is now named with aria-label and the image is
marked decorative.

A visually hidden span was deliberately not used here, although that is the
pattern elsewhere in this code base. The sort key of the group list is built
from every span inside every anchor of the row, so an extra span would end up in
it and could reorder the list - language dependently, because the added text is
the translated string.

The same markup is built a second time in JavaScript when a group is created
without a reload; both sites are fixed.

WCAG 2.1 AA, SC 4.1.2 and SC 1.1.1
